# The committed filter lists are build inputs whose exact bytes are recorded in
# filters/lists.lock.json. This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which
# would rewrite line endings on checkout and make every hash in the lock fail verification on
# a Linux CI runner. `-text` disables that conversion so the bytes on disk are the bytes that
# were downloaded, on every platform.
#
# `merge=binary` makes two refreshes of the same list conflict as whole files. A line merge
# interleaves hunks from two upstream snapshots into a list that matches neither (a pending
# refresh branch against a manual refresh hit 1,138 of them). Resolve by taking one side's
# filters/ wholesale, then `npm run check-lists` or `npm run lock-lists`.
filters/*.txt -text merge=binary
# The seed is ours, edited by hand: line merges are what we want there.
filters/quell-seed.txt merge

# Upstream lists, not our source. Collapses their diffs on GitHub by default (still
# expandable) and keeps them out of the repo's language statistics, so a refresh PR shows the
# lock summary rather than 40,000 lines of EasyList. Every list in filters/lists.json with a
# `url` belongs here; quell-seed.txt is ours.
filters/easylist.txt        linguist-generated=true
filters/easyprivacy.txt     linguist-generated=true
filters/easylist-cookie.txt linguist-generated=true
filters/easylist-china.txt  linguist-generated=true
filters/cjx-annoyance.txt   linguist-generated=true
filters/ubo-filters.txt     linguist-generated=true
filters/ubo-badware.txt     linguist-generated=true
filters/ubo-unbreak.txt     linguist-generated=true

# Redirect stand-ins that DNR serves byte for byte (regenerate with scripts/gen-redirect-media.mjs).
# Git already detects these as binary; this keeps autocrlf and diff away from them regardless.
src/redirects/*.gif binary
src/redirects/*.png binary
src/redirects/*.mp3 binary
src/redirects/*.mp4 binary
